# Optional pinned archive hashes for /usr/bin/spotify-soloist-updater.
#
# Spotify publishes no checksums or signatures for the Soloist archives, and the
# download URL always serves whatever build is current, so the only way to get a
# repeatable install is to pin the hash of an archive you have vetted yourself.
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#
#   <archive-name>  <sha256>
#
# Archive names, by mechanism (the spelling used in the URL):
#   arm64    aarch64, 64-bit ARM
#   arm32    armv7l / armv6l
#   x86_64   x86-64
#
# Example -- note that pinning a build also pins its expiry date, so a pinned
# entry stops being installable once that build passes 90 days:
#
#   x86_64  0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
#
# While every line stays commented out, the updater instead verifies the
# candidate by executing it before installation, which catches a wrong
# architecture and a missing shared library, but not a substituted payload.
